to step back up. And with the planning returns&nbsp;
we’ve had back and with October’s data, which I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:54.480 --> 00:43:01.440
did a first review of yesterday, you know, I still&nbsp;
feel comfortable that the envelopes we’ve got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:01.440 --> 00:43:06.080
are sufficient to allow the recovery of&nbsp;
activity even as we have seen some of the,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:06.800 --> 00:43:13.040
well, even as we’ve gone through in October, that&nbsp;
kind of first, the first signs of the second wave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:13.040 --> 00:43:22.960
we’ve definitely lived through in November.
On capital, anticipating the normal pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:22.960 --> 00:43:32.560
steep sort of hockey stick angle as we get into&nbsp;
the final quarter of the year reflecting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:32.560 --> 00:43:36.400
money that in particular we put out&nbsp;
there for increasing A&amp;E capacity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:38.400 --> 00:43:42.800
catching up with some of the critical&nbsp;
infrastructure, beginning the work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:42.800 --> 00:43:48.320
to get rid of mental health dormitories, where&nbsp;
as I think probably Simon said earlier, we’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:48.320 --> 00:43:53.520
had the second year’s funding for that programme&nbsp;
guaranteed in the SR announced earlier this week.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:53.520 --> 00:44:00.400
And I think Simon’s already covered the points on&nbsp;
the spending review. Happy to take any questions.&nbsp;

00:44:01.440 --> 00:44:04.960
&gt;&gt;David Prior: Can I just, one point on the&nbsp;
spending review? I mean, Simon did mention it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:04.960 --> 00:44:12.560
But the 330 billion I think that’s been earmarked&nbsp;
for diagnostics, which we discussed at the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:12.560 --> 00:44:16.240
board meeting in the light of Mike Richards’&nbsp;
report. I mean, how do you see that playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:16.240 --> 00:44:22.320
out over the next couple of years, Julian?
&gt;&gt;Julian Kelly: So, look, it’s a, I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:22.320 --> 00:44:26.560
first of all, I’d say it’s a positive sign that&nbsp;
the government have committed more funding to it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:26.560 --> 00:44:32.080
so we can get going. And we will need to have a&nbsp;
